# Example cron schedule -- a thin trigger that only says WHEN.
# Install with `crontab ops/scheduled/crontab.example` (edit paths/user first).
# The doer is scripts/jobs/review_docs.py -- this file holds no logic.
#
# ┌ minute ┌ hour ┌ day-of-month ┌ month ┌ day-of-week
# │        │      │              │       │

# Review the documentation every day at 02:00: stale `updated:` stamps and
# backticked paths that resolve to nothing, as JSON, for whoever reads the log.
0 2 * * * cd /path/to/repo && python3 scripts/jobs/review_docs.py --json > /var/log/keel/doc-review.json

# systemd-timer equivalent (same doer): [Timer] OnCalendar=*-*-* 02:00:00
# CI equivalent (shipped): .github/workflows/scheduled.yml -- a `schedule` trigger
# calling the same script. Same doer, different cadence adapter (CONVENTIONS §7).
